# 🎭 Playwright + Cucumber BDD Framework

A practice-based test automation framework built with **Playwright** and **Cucumber BDD** using **JavaScript (ESM)**.

> ⚠️ This framework is NOT an end-to-end application test suite.
> It is a **learning-focused** implementation covering individual UI interaction scenarios to build strong Playwright fundamentals.

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

| Tool | Purpose |
|---|---|
| [Playwright](https://playwright.dev/) | Browser automation |
| [Cucumber BDD](https://cucumber.io/) | Gherkin feature files + step definitions |
| JavaScript (Module) | Language — using `import` throughout |
| Node `assert` | Built-in assertions — no extra libraries |
| Cucumber HTML Reporter | Auto-generated local HTML report |

## ⚙️ Setup and Installation

**1. Clone the repository**
```bash
git clone [your repo link]
cd playwright-bdd-framework
```

**2. Install dependencies**
```bash
npm install
```

**3. Install Playwright browsers**
```bash
npx playwright install
```

---

## ▶️ Running Tests

**Run all scenarios:**
```bash
npm test
```

**Run by tag:**
```bash
npx cucumber-js --tags "@input"
npx cucumber-js --tags "@dropdown"
npx cucumber-js --tags "@radiobutton"
```

**Run with HTML report:**
```bash
npm run test:report
```

---

## 📊 Reports

After every run an HTML report is auto-generated at:
```
reports/cucumber-report.html
```
Open it in any browser to view results.

